  "page1": {
    "title": "The Secret of Factors",
    "subtitle": "Share cookies and count by fours to meet factors and multiples.",
    "body": "Mina has 12 cookies. She wants to share them equally. She can give them to 2, 3, 4, or 6 friends. Each friend then gets the same number. These numbers are the factors of 12.\n\nA factor divides a number with nothing left over. So the factors of 12 are 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, and 12.\n\nNow count by fours. We get 4, 8, 12, 16, and 20. These are the multiples of 4. A multiple grows when you add the same number again.\n\nA number that <mark>divides two numbers</mark> is their common factor. The factors of 12 and 18 share 1, 2, 3, and 6. So factors split a number, and multiples build it up. Math hides many neat patterns.",
